 #:seon.task{:name "the-test-step-writes-nothing-on-main"
  :kind :function
  :intent "Phase P3 of hybrid-step-semantics.md (F2; AGENTS.md: agents are compartments). `seon.turn/record-reached-red!` judges the agent's change through `seon.test/change-reds`, which acquires main (`seon.turn/root-execution`), runs the tests main lacks there and records them in main's custody (`seon.db/call-with-custody` on main) from the agent's pass. Correct: one pure rule, `seon.context/step-status`, judges the step against its fork point (`:seon.task.attempt/fork`, else main's head when the attempt was written) inside the agent's compartment: broken = a reaching test that existed at the fork point, was not red there and is red at the head; new-red = red at the head and absent there, never breakage (a Prove step's product). Only the reaching tests red at the head need a baseline: the evidence the branch inherited at the fork point (readable after P1), else one run in the fork commit's program context recorded on the agent's branch. `record-broken!` writes `:seon.agent/broken` on the branch; `seon.turn/reached-red`, `record-reached-red!` and the main run go. Proofs: seon.turn-test/the-test-step-writes-nothing-on-main (main's basis unchanged across a pass that broke a test); seon.context-test/each-step-kind-is-done-by-its-one-rule (table); seon.cluster.db-flow-test/a-prove-steps-red-proof-for-its-successor-is-not-a-reached-red (chain-experiment-1-proofs.patch, p declared :prove). Files: src/seon/turn.clj, src/seon/test.clj, src/seon/context.clj, test/seon/turn_test.clj, test/seon/context_test.clj, test/seon/cluster/db_flow_test.clj."
  :must-read #{seon.turn/test-step seon.turn/record-broken! seon.test/fork-point-red seon.context/step-status seon.context/task-done?}
  :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/hybrid-step-semantics.md" "docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-1.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-merge-request-comes-only-from-a-step-no-task-needs"
