  :intent "`seon.turn/show-row` passes `(or source \"\")` as `:seon.cluster.eval/source` to `seon.sci.eval/shown-failure`, whose request schema `:seon.sci.eval/shown-request` requires a string of length at least 1, so showing a failed entry with no source records a fault instead of the failure: signature f7755aef71c0d6c2d3a531fd42b8fa7c013db6726fd9fd479e5caeb65c5fd166 on default 2319152dc, agent attempt/e95d4e90b70f, 2026-10-12T00:23:45Z (chain experiment 1, F6). Find which entry reaches show-row without source (a reply that is only tool markup, or a step-run entry), and fix at the producer: the entry carries its source, or the request schema admits its absence as no key; never an empty string."
